  "description": "Part single, part 2-storey rear extension with increase to roof height.",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its inadequate floor area would result in substandard and inappropriate accommodation incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed first and second floor rear extensions, by virtue of their sitting, projection and proximity to the site boundary would give rise to an give rise to an unneighbourly loss of loss of daylight and sunlight and outlook, as perceived from the neighbouring property, No.508 Hertford Road, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD8 and DMD11 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of adequate waste storage, would fail to provide a convenient and accessible facility for managing waste generated by the development. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T4 and T7 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP22 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) Policies DMD8, DMD30 and DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the Enfield Waste and Recycling Storage Planning Guidance (2020)."
  ],
